WEBVTT

00:00:01.372 --> 00:00:07.152
On October 18th, 1960, speaking in Shemokin, Pennsylvania, when he was running for vice president.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.860
Lyndon Johnson said,

00:00:09.564 --> 00:00:14.164
I don't want some bearded dictator 90 miles off thumbing his nose at us.

00:00:14.428 --> 00:00:15.148
End the quote.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.860
Now to debate Mr. Johnson on this statement.

00:00:18.204 --> 00:00:19.584
Here is Barry Goldwater.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:24.868
who calls him to account for this administration's colossal bungling on Cuba and Castro.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.980
The same bearded dictator is still 90 miles off thumbing his nose

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.500
at us

00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:32.848
And the Bay of Pigs has left us.

00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:34.564
Not a monument to freedom.

00:00:35.052 --> 00:00:37.332
but a dark blot on our national pride.

00:00:37.836 --> 00:00:39.876
The United States must provide the leadership.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.472
which will deal effectively with the problems of Cuba.

00:00:42.988 --> 00:00:46.268
and which will stop the spread of communism in the Western Hemisphere.

00:00:47.084 --> 00:00:47.784
In your heart.

00:00:47.916 --> 00:00:48.956
You know he's right.

00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:50.684
Vote for Barry Goldwater.
